v3d: don't load the destination of a blit that overwrites all of it

A render blit draws into a job that loads the destination into the tile buffer first unless the
destination is known to be undefined. When the blit writes every pixel of a single-level,
single-layer colour destination (no scissor, no window rectangles, no active render condition, no
blending, every channel), its earlier contents cannot show: the destination is invalidated before
the blit, so its job clears the tiles instead of loading them, and a pending job's store of it is
dropped. An app's final full-window copy (Godot's, Waze's map) hits this every frame; the window's
back buffer is otherwise loaded although nothing of it survives.

Measured on a Pi 4 (stock clocks), Waze's car map at 1184x928: 26.1/26.5 -> 26.8/27.2 frames/s
(with mesa-v3d-vs-texture-bin-sync.patch: 27.6/28.0). tools/debian/v3d-mesa-test.c checks that a
blit over the whole destination gives exactly the blit's pixels and one over part of it keeps the
rest, with the destination drawn into just before.

Applies to Mesa 26.3.1 (tools/debvm/versions.env MESA_*), patch -p1 in the source tree.

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/v3d/v3d_blit.c b/src/gallium/drivers/v3d/v3d_blit.c
index 7317a4120a0..4cf76c3d201 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/v3d/v3d_blit.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/v3d/v3d_blit.c
@@ -138,6 +138,31 @@ v3d_render_blit(struct pipe_context *ctx, struct pipe_blit_info *info)

         MESA_TRACE_FUNC();

+        /* A colour blit that writes every pixel of a single-level, single-
+         * layer destination makes its earlier contents irrelevant: mark it
+         * invalidated, so the blit's job neither loads them into the tile
+         * buffer nor waits for a store of them (an app's final copy into its
+         * window, every frame).  Not when a scissor, window rectangles, a
+         * render condition (which can skip the blit), blending or a partial
+         * channel mask could leave pixels of the destination as they were.
+         */
+        struct pipe_resource *pdst = info->dst.resource;
+        if (pdst != info->src.resource &&
+            !util_format_is_depth_or_stencil(info->dst.format) &&
+            (info->mask & PIPE_MASK_RGBA) == PIPE_MASK_RGBA &&
+            !info->scissor_enable && !info->num_window_rectangles &&
+            !info->alpha_blend &&
+            !(info->render_condition_enable && v3d->cond_query) &&
+            pdst->last_level == 0 && pdst->array_size == 1 &&
+            pdst->depth0 == 1 && pdst->nr_samples <= 1 &&
+            info->dst.level == 0 &&
+            info->dst.box.x == 0 && info->dst.box.y == 0 &&
+            info->dst.box.z == 0 && info->dst.box.depth == 1 &&
+            info->dst.box.width == pdst->width0 &&
+            info->dst.box.height == pdst->height0) {
+                ctx->invalidate_resource(ctx, pdst);
+        }
+
         v3d_blitter_save(v3d, info->render_condition_enable ?
                          V3D_BLIT_COND : V3D_BLIT);
         util_blitter_blit(v3d->blitter, info, NULL);
